","file":"preprints/Nagatas-Conjecture-for-Plane-Curves-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":31,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"f4b52209377824aa9578b7b04e0e61a19105961a3b0b13cc53b7b7bd4bf08e6b","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Nagatas-Conjecture-for-Plane-Curves-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:2db5e5562ff1f8e26d16739a7e2b6be493fc6912ff0ecc137954bdcc22402e64","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Nagatas-Conjecture-for-Plane-Curves-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L31"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every integer $r\\ge10$, there is a countable union $E_r$ of proper\nZariski-closed subsets of $U_r$, with nonempty complement, such that the\nfollowing holds for every tuple $(p_1,\\ldots,p_r)\\notin E_r$.\nIf $C$ is a nonzero effective plane curve of degree $d\\ge1$ and\n$m_1,\\ldots,m_r\\in\\Z_{\\ge0}$ satisfy $\\mult_{p_i}C\\ge m_i$, then\n\\[\n d\\sqrt r>\\sum_{i=1}^r m_i.\n\\]"}
